<title>HONG KONG: Ocean-Land says H1 net loss at HK$12 mln.</title>
<headline>Ocean-Land says H1 net loss at HK$12 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended September 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 15.0 loss  vs 20.0 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  2.0	  vs 13.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	nil	  vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			  11.97 loss vs 15.89 profit (see note)</p>
<p>    Turnover		   119.62     vs 369.45</p>
<p>    Company name	     Ocean-Land Development Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		February 1-5</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 February 11</p>
<p>NOTE - Ocean-Land is an investment holding company with subsidiaries engaged in shipping, property and investment.</p>
<p>Comparative figures has been restated to include HK$8.58 million being write back of provision in diminution in value of private capital fund which was grouped under exceptional items last year.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
